WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
A happy cottage girl.

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:07.950
Then a lord comes by, and she asks: "Why
did a great lord find me out," He takes

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.460
her to his palace.

4
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.710
Then he sees someone
else: her cousin, Kate.

5
00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.290
Kate gets the ring.

6
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.810
The speaker is left outside the gate.

7
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:22.730
Then the last stanza turns: "Yet I've
a gift you have not got," One woman has

8
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:23.590
the ring.

9
00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.020
One has a gift.

10
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.100
So who has really won?

11
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.090
In this mission, you'll meet the
Victorian idea of the fallen woman,

12
00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.440
and the double standard behind it.

13
00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:36.940
You'll follow the story of the
lord, the speaker and Kate,

14
00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:38.560
stanza by stanza.

15
00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.940
And you'll pin down the
turn in that last stanza.

16
00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.600
Your mission: decide who has won.
